Q: How to generate signature in Shopee 2.0 API request authentication? A: <p>Here's my helper I used to generate the signature. If you inspect the Shopee OP docs, you will notice that some sign requires more params (Private APIs) while some require less (Public APIs). This fn can help facilitate both.</p>
<pre><code>public static function buildSignature(string $path, bool $public = false, ?int $timestamp = null): string
    {
        $timestamp = $timestamp ?? time();
        return hash_hmac(
            'sha256',
            env('SHOPEE_PARTNER_ID') . 
            $path . 
            $timestamp ?? time() . 
            ($public ? &quot;&quot; : Cache::get('shopee.auth.access_token', null)) . 
            ($public ? &quot;&quot; : Cache::get('shopee.auth.shop_id', null)),
            env('SHOPEE_PARTNER_KEY')
        );
    }
</code></pre>
<p>Example:</p>
<p>To use at an public endpoint, you may use it like this:</p>
<pre><code>$sign = buildSignature('/api/v2/auth/token/get', true)

// pass timestamp if you need to sync it with other parts of your request.
$sign = buildSignature('/api/v2/auth/token/get', true, $timestamp)
</code></pre>

